  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Epic singing of the Uzbek baxshis of Surkhandarya and Kashkadarya in southern Uzbekistan, who perform dostons such as Alpamysh in alternating prose and verse, accompanying themselves on the two-string dombra, for which the dombyra card stands. The southern school is known for bo'g'iq ovoz, a deep, muffled throat voice; UNESCO has proclaimed the cultural space of Boysun District and inscribed the bakhshi art of Uzbekistan.",
